<title>UK: Bat to consider US tobacco claim settlement.</title>
<headline>Bat to consider US tobacco claim settlement.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>B.A.T Industries Plc said on Wednesday it is now time to evaluate a possible settlement of a string of U.S. tobacco-related lawsuits, B.A.T chief executive Martin Broughton told reporters.</p>
<p>&quot;The on-going cost in legal terms, and the impact on the share price is such that we think it sensible and appropriate to evaluate a settlement,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>He put the legal costs at $100 million in 1996, which he expected to rise at least over the next two years.</p>
</text>
